@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "koroneiki.integration"

Feature:  Koroneiki To Provisioning License Integration
	Testing to assure that koroneiki account integration to provisioning and License Management works properly.

Teardown:
	* I wait for "10" seconds
	* I tear down the product purchases on koroneiki made by the account "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" for the following products with their respective field values
	| Digital Enterprise Production | startDate | ${staticStartDate}       |
	| Digital Enterprise Production | startDate | ${staticFutureStartDate} |
	* I tear down the product purchases on koroneiki made by the account "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" for the following products
	| Digital Enterprise Production            |
	| Digital Enterprise Backup                |
	| Digital Enterprise Non-Production        |
	| Portal Production                        |
	| Platinum Subscription                    |
	| Gold Subscription                        |
	| Limited Subscription                     |
	| Enterprise Search for DXP Cloud - Prod   |
	| Liferay Commerce Subscription Production |
	| Developer Services                       |
	| Liferay Analytics Cloud Basic            |
	| Enterprise Search - Production           |
	* I tear down the product consumptions on koroneiki made by the account "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" for the following products
	| Digital Enterprise Production |
	| Portal Production             |
	* I tear down the products on koroneiki with the following names
	| Platinum Subscription |
	| Gold Subscription     |
	| Limited Subscription  |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following names
	| Korone - ${staticProjectName} |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following "Code" values
	| KORONEKORONE |

Scenario: Generate new DXP license via provisioning site
	Testing the ability to generate a new license for a regular DXP project from koroneiki via the provisioning site

	Given I generate a provisioning project name
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                  | KORONEKORONE                         |
	| Contact Email Address | osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Description           | Test osb account on koroneiki        |
	| Fax Number            | 555-555-1234                         |
	| Name                  | Korone - ${staticProjectName}        |
	| Phone Number          | 555-555-5678                         |
	| Profile Email Address | osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Region                | United States                        |
	| Status                | Approved                             |
	| Tier                  | Regular                              |
	| Website               | www.koroneikicorporation.com         |
	And I generate the account key value for "Korone - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I generate static start and end dates
	And I generate static full start and end dates
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Digital Enterprise Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         |   |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} |   |
	| Perpetual               | false                    |   |
	| Product Field and Value | sizing                   | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | licenses                 | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | version                  | 7 |
	| Quantity                | 1                        |   |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       |   |
	| Status                  | Approved                 |   |
	And I generate the product purchase ID value for the product purchase made by "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" for "Digital Enterprise Production"
	And I create a product with the following values
	| Name | Platinum Subscription | |
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Platinum Subscription" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                    | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I log into the support homepage as "amos.fong@liferay.com.broken" with password "test" on the sandbox
	And I log into the provisioning homepage as "test@liferay.com" with password "kwSgiajslgb7ecsD"
	And I search the accounts page using the keyword "Korone"
	And I click on the account with the name "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" on the provisioning index
	And I click on the "Digital Enterprise Production" subscription link
	And I click on generate license button
	And I generate a new license with the following values
	| Product                | Digital Enterprise Production              | |
	| Choose Liferay Version | 7.2                                        | |
	| Type                   | Digital Enterprise Production (Production) | |
	| Choose Purchase        | ${staticProductPurchaseId}                 | |
	| Host Name              | localhost                                  | |
	| IP Addresses           | 123.456.789.012                            | |
	| MAC Addresses          | 0A-1B-2C-3D-4E-5F                          | |
	And I go to the License Management page on sandbox
	And I search the License Management page with the account key value "${staticAccountKey}"
	Then I should be able to view the license with the name "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" following values
	| Project         | KORONE                            |
	| Name            | Korone - ${staticProjectName}     |
	| Product         | Digital Enterprise Production 7.2 |
	| Type            | Production                        |
	And I should be able to view a product consumption on koroneiki made by the account "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" for the product "Digital Enterprise Production" with the following values
	| End Date   | ${staticEndDate}   | |
	| Start Date | ${staticStartDate} | |
	When I go to the account index page
	And I search the accounts page using the keyword "Korone"
	And I click on the account with the name "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" on the provisioning index
	Then I should be able to view the product with the name "Digital Enterprise Production" and the following values on the account details page
	| Name         | Digital Enterprise Production |
	| Provisioned  | 1                             |
	| Status       | ACTIVE                        |

Scenario: Deactivate new DXP license via provisioning site
	Testing the ability to generate and deactivate new license for a regular DXP project from koroneiki via the provisioning site

	Given I generate a provisioning project name
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                  | KORONEKORONE                         |
	| Contact Email Address | osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Description           | Test osb account on koroneiki        |
	| Fax Number            | 555-555-1234                         |
	| Name                  | Korone - ${staticProjectName}        |
	| Phone Number          | 555-555-5678                         |
	| Profile Email Address | osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Region                | United States                        |
	| Status                | Approved                             |
	| Tier                  | Regular                              |
	| Website               | www.koroneikicorporation.com         |
	And I generate the account key value for "Korone - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I generate static start and end dates
	And I generate static full start and end dates
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Digital Enterprise Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         |   |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} |   |
	| Perpetual               | false                    |   |
	| Product Field and Value | sizing                   | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | licenses                 | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | version                  | 7 |
	| Quantity                | 1                        |   |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       |   |
	| Status                  | Approved                 |   |
	And I generate the product purchase ID value for the product purchase made by "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" for "Digital Enterprise Production"
	And I create a product with the following values
	| Name | Platinum Subscription | |
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Platinum Subscription" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                    | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I log into the support homepage as "amos.fong@liferay.com.broken" with password "test" on the sandbox
	And I log into the provisioning homepage as "test@liferay.com" with password "kwSgiajslgb7ecsD"
	And I search the accounts page using the keyword "Korone"
	And I click on the account with the name "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" on the provisioning index
	And I click on the "Digital Enterprise Production" subscription link
	And I click on generate license button
	And I generate a new license with the following values
	| Product                | Digital Enterprise Production              | |
	| Choose Liferay Version | 7.2                                        | |
	| Type                   | Digital Enterprise Production (Production) | |
	| Choose Purchase        | ${staticProductPurchaseId}                 | |
	| Host Name              | localhost                                  | |
	| IP Addresses           | 123.456.789.012                            | |
	| MAC Addresses          | 0A-1B-2C-3D-4E-5F                          | |
	And I go to the License Management page on sandbox
	And I search the License Management page with the account key value "${staticAccountKey}"
	And I click on the license with the name "Korone - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I click on the deactivate link
	And I wait for "5" seconds
	Then I should not be able to view a product consumption on koroneiki made by the account "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" for the product "Digital Enterprise Production"
	When I go to the account index page
	And I search the accounts page using the keyword "Korone"
	And I click on the account with the name "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" on the provisioning index
	Then I should be able to view the product with the name "Digital Enterprise Production" and the following values on the account details page
	| Name         | Digital Enterprise Production |
	| Provisioned  | 0                             |
	| Status       | ACTIVE                        |

